        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: निष्ठुर",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "निष्ठुर — niṣṭhur — \"heartless; unfeeling\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बच्चा रो रहा था, लेकिन वह निष्ठुर आदमी नहीं रुका। baccā ro rahā thā, lekin vah niṣṭhur ādmī nahīṃ rukā. The child was crying, but that heartless man didn't stop."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "निष्ठुर (niṣṭhur) is a tatsama, borrowed from Sanskrit niṣṭhura, \"hard, rough, harsh, cruel\", said especially of words (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
